From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:28:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [declarative] Fix recordings, reconnection and conference
 state.

Call recorder:
- The remote party's name and id became part of the file name as they
  were, so a name holding '/' or ".." wrote the recording elsewhere or
  failed, and a long name exceeded NAME_MAX. Replace separators and
  control characters, no leading dots, and cap each part in UTF-8 bytes.
- deleteRecording() took any path relative to the recordings directory,
  "../" included. Accept plain file names only.
- The WAV header said 16-bit PCM while unsigned samples were requested,
  and described the requested format rather than the one the device
  gave. Ask for signed samples and write the header from the actual
  format, with 64-bit length math, refusing data that does not fit.
- The rename of the finished file was not checked, so callRecorded()
  named a file that might not exist. An empty recording left a 44-byte
  file behind; remove it.
- stop() emits stateChanged(StoppedState), which re-entered
  terminateRecording() while it tore the input down. Disconnect first.

Manager and call handler:
- initialize() retried every two seconds with the same QDBusInterface,
  which never becomes valid once introspection failed, so a QML client
  started before voicecall-manager never connected; and each retry
  created another Ngf client. Recreate the interface, create the Ngf
  client once.
- The active call was looked up before the call model was filled, and
  kept as a raw pointer the model could delete. Fill the model first,
  hold it in a QPointer.
- remoteHeld changes emitted the property getter's name instead of
  remoteHeldChanged().
- A call that became a conference after setup never got a model of its
  members.
- Watchers of successful pending calls were never deleted.

recordingfile.h holds the name and header handling so that
tst_recordingfile can test it without audio or D-Bus.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
